.TH LOAM 1 "2026-11-23" "loam 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
loam \- native runtime for Soil WebAssembly components
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B loam
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B loam
is the native host for Soil components. It runs installed WebAssembly
components, links the capabilities they were granted, and keeps the signed
package boundary. It is not the Soil compiler, REPL, formatter, or language
server.
.PP
Installed command and Spore packages are discovered under
.I ~/.local/share/fungos/commands
and
.IR ~/.local/share/fungos/spores .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run \fINAME\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
Run an installed command component. This is the virtual PATH; it does not
compile or interpret Soil source.
.TP
.B install \fIPATH\fR [\fB\-\-root\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-allow-unsigned-dev\fR]
Verify, compose, warm, and atomically install a package. The install is
source-preserving and keeps generations for rollback.
.TP
.B status [\fB\-\-root\fR \fIDIR\fR]... [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Show managed installs from the default roots.
.TP
.B rollback \fIID\fR [\fB\-\-root\fR \fIDIR\fR]
Switch an install back one generation.
.TP
.B image plan \fIPATH\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Build the granted WIT and provider host plan for an image Spore.
.TP
.B surface \fIFILE\fR [\fB\-\-size\fR \fIWxH\fR] [\fB\-\-capture\fR \fIFILE\fR]
Open a native surface or capture one frame.
.TP
.B plugin \fIlist\fR|\fIverify\fR|\fIinspect\fR|\fIroots\fR|\fIpack\fR|\fIcompose\fR
Inspect, seal, or compose Spore capability exports.
.TP
.B edit \fIopen\fR|\fIread\fR|\fIlist\fR|\fIcheckpoint\fR|\fIsave\fR|\fIapply\fR
Edit a personal source overlay without mutating the signed package.
.TP
.B doctor
Print the runtime version and linked capability profile.
.TP
.B help
Print command help.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/loam/loam.conf.soil
Per-user host defaults for the daemon. Command-line flags override the file.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/loam/logs/
Durable per-instance logs, rotated by size.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/loam/loamd.sock
Default local control socket for
.BR loamd (1).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FUNGOS_COMMAND_ROOT
Override the command package root.
.TP
.B LOAM_CONFIG
Path to a host configuration file.
.TP
.B MYCELIUM_HOME
Mycelium state directory used for identity and service leases.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run an installed command:
.PP
.nf
loam run hello --name world
.fi
.PP
Install a local package and inspect it:
.PP
.nf
loam install ./hello
loam status --json
.fi
.PP
Open a surface:
.PP
.nf
loam surface hello.wasm --size 1000x700
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR loamd (1),
.BR soil (1),
.BR wasmtime (1)
